@startuml
!include common-style.puml

title Use Case Diagram — Phase 2 (Part 2)\nServices, Lab, Inventory, Pharmacy, Extended Billing

top to bottom direction

actor Admin #DBEAFE
actor Doctor #DCFCE7
actor "Lab Technician" as LabTech #FCE7F3
actor Pharmacist #FEE2E2
actor Cashier #FFEDD5
actor Manager #F3E8FF

rectangle "4N Clinic — Lab, Pharmacy & Extended Operations" {

  package "Service & Lab Orders" {
    usecase "UC25\nOrder clinic service" as UC25
    usecase "UC26\nCreate lab test order" as UC26
    usecase "UC27\nCollect sample" as UC27
    usecase "UC28\nEnter lab result" as UC28
    usecase "UC29\nVerify lab result" as UC29
  }

  package "Inventory & Pharmacy" {
    usecase "UC30\nReceive drug lot" as UC30
    usecase "UC31\nTrack stock / expiry" as UC31
    usecase "UC32\nDispense drugs (FEFO)" as UC32
  }

  package "Extended Billing & Reports" {
    usecase "UC33\nMulti-item invoice" as UC33
    usecase "UC34\nExtended reports" as UC34
  }
}

Doctor --> UC25
Doctor --> UC26
Doctor --> UC29

LabTech --> UC27
LabTech --> UC28
LabTech --> UC29

Pharmacist --> UC30
Pharmacist --> UC31
Pharmacist --> UC32

Cashier --> UC33

Manager --> UC34
Admin --> UC30
Admin --> UC34

UC26 .> UC25 : lab is a service
UC27 .> UC26 : <<include>>
UC28 .> UC27 : after sample collected
UC29 .> UC28 : verify result
UC32 .> UC31 : FEFO lot selection
UC33 .> UC25 : service line items
UC33 .> UC32 : drug line items

note bottom of UC32
FEFO = First Expired, First Out.
Lots with earliest expiry date
are consumed first.
end note

@enduml
